From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: drd: gate the pull-up on role for glues without pre_set_role

With dr_mode "otg" and a usb-role-switch, USB_ROLE_NONE maps to the
peripheral default mode, so dwc3_set_mode() is a no-op on detach and the
gadget keeps D+ pulled up. dwc3-qcom-legacy has no pre_set_role hook and
forces the VBUS override on, so the controller never sees the session
end. Tell the UDC core about VBUS from the role instead.

(Carried over from the re-plug analysis; needed once usb_1/usb_2 become
role-switched OTG ports.)

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c	2026-09-26 02:31:55.603449337 +0200
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c	2026-09-26 02:31:55.615548194 +0200
@@ -470,6 +470,25 @@
 
 	dwc3_pre_set_role(dwc, role);
 	dwc3_set_mode(dwc, mode);
+
+	/*
+	 * USB_ROLE_NONE maps to the peripheral default mode, so for a
+	 * device-only port dwc3_set_mode() above is a no-op and the gadget
+	 * would keep D+ pulled up across detach/attach. Glues without a
+	 * pre_set_role hook (e.g. dwc3-qcom-legacy, whose VBUS override is
+	 * forced on) never tell the controller the session ended. Gate the
+	 * pull-up on the role instead: NONE drops it, DEVICE restores it via
+	 * pullup(1) -> soft reset + run/stop, after the Type-C/charger side has
+	 * settled.
+	 */
+	if (!(dwc->glue_ops && dwc->glue_ops->pre_set_role)) {
+		mutex_lock(&dwc->mutex);
+		if (dwc->current_dr_role == DWC3_GCTL_PRTCAP_DEVICE &&
+		    mode == DWC3_GCTL_PRTCAP_DEVICE && dwc->gadget)
+			usb_udc_vbus_handler(dwc->gadget, role == USB_ROLE_DEVICE);
+		mutex_unlock(&dwc->mutex);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
